{"name":"Roast Beetroot Dahl","permalink":"roast-beetroot-dahl","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/RoastBeetrootDahl.scala","source":"Hello Fresh","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":["The beetroot quantity is guestimated. Will refine over time.","We use a modified version of <a href=\"https://www.theflavorbender.com/sri-lankan-roasted-curry-powder/\">this</a> Sri Lankan Curry power recipe. Will write down our version some time."],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Vegan","Spicy","Scales"],"inherited_tags":["Pescatarian","Vegetarian-ish","Vegetarian","Vegan-ish"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Beetroot","quantity":"500g","prep":"cut into 2cm chunks","notes":null},{"name":"Onion","quantity":"1","prep":"thinly sliced","notes":null},{"name":"Spring Onions","quantity":"2","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Lime","quantity":"1","prep":"zested and juiced","notes":null},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"2 cloves","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Flatbreads","quantity":"4","prep":null,"notes":"Optional"},{"name":"Sri Lankan Curry Powder","quantity":"a few tablespoons","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Stock cube","quantity":"1","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Coconut Milk","quantity":"1 400ml tin","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Red Lentils","quantity":"150g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Water","quantity":"200ml","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Oil","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Preheat the oven to 200°C (390°F, gas mark 6).","Spread the beetroot on a baking tray. Drizzle with oil and season with salt and pepper.","Roast the beetroot for 20-25 minutes then set aside.","Boil the water and make stock.","Heat a large saucepan with some oil. Add the onions and soften for a few minutes.","Stir in the curry powder and garlic then cook for a minute.","Add the coconut milk, lentils and stock, then bring to the boil.","Turn down the heat and simmer for 20-25 minutes or until the lentils are soft. Stir every few minutes.","Mix the roasted beetroot and lime juice into the lentils.","Lightly toast the flatbreads.","Serve with a garnish of lime zest and spring onions, with the flatbreads on the side."]}